    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by high-upside matchups, led by **Kyle Schwarber** (75.96) and **Trea Turner** (75.57). Both benefit significantly from facing Ryan Johnson, whose 5.16 xERA represents the most favorable pitching environment on our board. **Trea Turner** remains our premier engine for stolen bases, and despite a minor projected penalty for the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time, his premium spot in the order maximizes his efficiency. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.50) and **Christian Yelich** (72.07) round out our top-tier plays; **Christian Yelich** is particularly intriguing against Cal Quantrill, as the dynamic platoon advantage coupled with Quantrill\u2019s slow delivery creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the basepaths.\n\nEfficiency across the board is bolstered by several favorable situational factors, most notably for **Junior Caminero** (68.13), who overcomes a slight park penalty to maintain elite status due to a strong projected spot in the lineup. **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.48) also provides a stable anchor, gaining value from his platoon advantage against Anderson. The most difficult personnel decision centered on **Carson Benge**, who finished just outside the starting rotation with a score of 46.21. While his base metrics are respectable, he was sidelined in favor of higher-efficiency options who benefit more from specific park factors or superior lineup positioning.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key contributors. Should **Gary Sanchez** or **Lars Nootbaar** see their batting order significantly demoted once official lineups are posted, their daily efficiency scores will slide toward the marginal threshold, potentially necessitating a re-evaluation of our bench utilization. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Dillon Dingler** (51.53), as his utility is tethered to the projected platoon edge against Snell; any late-scratch or tactical defensive substitution for the opposition could compress his output. We are proceeding with our current configuration, keeping **Colt Keith** on the bench due to his lack of a confirmed start.",
